@tas50 the current method will suffer from the same issue I've complained about since Chef 14.

Let's say I want to make an administrator _think_ I have automatic updates turned on. Instead of passing a boolean value of `True` to  the `AutomaticallyInstallMacOSUpdates` key, I will instead pass an integer of `1`. As coded (and previously coded) chef will see this value, and happily move on. Unlike macos_userdefaults, Apple will reject this key and not honor the value, defaulting to `False`.

To me, this fundamentally means the DSC model for this resource is broken. Given that administrators may depend on this resource for critical security functionality, I think it would be prudent to ensure it properly compares the values, even at the expense of resource speed.
